{"title":"2025 CEMC Hypatia Problems/Problem 4c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Hypatia Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <i>geometric</i> sequence is a sequence in which each term after the first is obtained from the previous term by multiplying it by a non-zero constant, called the <i>common ratio</i>. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/455e64dfca6a85a26a7b425a8df331c412a8466b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5, 10, 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" /> is a geometric sequence with three terms and a common ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_4c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine all quadruples of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8c31b328eb3b0252134a4720e161c0fdf641e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c, d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c06de735d79f0b28c30bcbbcf96e67bb1ca42c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c, d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is a geometric sequence and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/9/ca90c2a32345ba95c89549319d9215fc8ca956d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c + d = 65$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_4c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_4c&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the common ratio. We then see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/1/dd1b04e461c26258947b86a40a36b69638b41bb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = ar$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/a/59a08f5307010d803e332ef999dffed3f8cc859f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = ar^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/4184469769962b52c0fc30cce20602d259b4bea3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = ar^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />. The sum would then be:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238779a6a4ca4fbb13cbc99e0b37a3d55b812fa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65 = a + ar + ar^{2} + ar^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"190\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/1294076c2985e9f79ec20ac263d6b645c8774aa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65 = a(1 + r + r^{2} + r^{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"185\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea1a8ae5c36109880fb539a920e922b454bb1a68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65 = a(1(1 + r) + r^{2}(1 + r)) = a(1 + r)(1 + r^{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"373\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>We could have also reached this conclusion from the formula for the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> numbers of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometric_sequence\" title=\"Geometric sequence\">geometric sequence</a>:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67a401968963013824fcfe481bbb30fdeca86cda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n = \\frac{a_1(r^{n} - 1)}{r - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"131\" height=\"42\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a070eea97d9363f58a257e05e75fc69efa753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> represents the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> terms, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /><sup>th</sup> term of the sequence, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the common ratio. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5218af40079081e694d8b82eeac2d368ef6ea76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cd1990ea279ef93b36b0678f0013fa8581fe3d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/905559f0ddcf63c6d8844479e3430c75d6d8f7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_4 = 65$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" />, so we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/6/9561a08fc22c58a89f4e8a2277261c430ab7e0fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_4 = \\frac{a(r^{4} - 1)}{r - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"120\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/96195e5e0a0bf3d7eb35e793980d23f7633e4583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65 = \\frac{a(r^{2} - 1)(r^{2} + 1)}{r - 1} = \\frac{a(r - 1)(r + 1)(r^{2} + 1)}{r - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"389\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7059aeea588b558c7e9399c6cb42f406b65044.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65 = a(r + 1)(r^{2} + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018032332\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.093 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 97/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 857/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4625/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.027      1 -total\n 45.98%    6.909      1 2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_4\n 38.83%    5.835      1 Template:Solution\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36327:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018032332 and revision id 281363. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}